%description:

Tcp.minRexmitTimeout:binds -- the RTO is the minimum when the estimate is smaller.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the lower limit of the retransmission timeout (RFC 6298 section 2.4:
1 s; Linux: 200 ms)".

The classes: binds (a minimum above SRTT + 4 RTTVAR; 1s is the default) and free (a minimum
below it; 200ms is the value of LinuxTcp), on a path whose round trip is 100 ms. The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::rttMeasurementComplete(). This test separates "binds" from "free".

Host under test: host1, which sends 10000 bytes on a path with a round trip of 100 ms. The
first measurement gives SRTT = 0.1 s and RTTVAR = 0.05 s, so the estimate is 0.3 s.
Observation: level 2, the signal rto after the first measurement is 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.minRexmitTimeout
%# class: binds
%# value: 1s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMinRexmitTimeoutBinds")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("rto")
                  .first()
                  .assertValueBetween(0.99, 1.01)
                  .describe("the RTO after the first measurement, the minimum")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMinRexmitTimeoutBinds compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.minRexmitTimeout = 1s    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 25ms
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMinRexmitTimeoutBinds: PASS
